# AI-Based Automatic Question Generation System

## 📌 Project Overview

The **AI-Based Automatic Question Generation System** is an NLP and Machine Learning application that automatically generates questions from uploaded educational documents.

The system accepts documents in different formats, extracts the content, and uses an AI language model to generate questions based on the selected question type and difficulty level.

The generated questions are further analyzed using Machine Learning models to classify question type, difficulty, similarity, and quality.

---

## ✨ Features

* 📄 Upload educational documents
* 📚 Support for PDF, DOCX, TXT, and PPTX files
* 🤖 AI-based automatic question generation
* 🌐 Support for Myanmar, Pali, and English
* ❓ Multiple question types
* 🎯 Difficulty-level selection
* 🔍 Duplicate/similarity detection
* 📊 Machine Learning-based question analysis
* 📝 Export generated questions
* 🖥️ Interactive Gradio Web Interface

---

## 🧠 Question Types

The system can generate:

* Multiple Choice Questions (MCQ)
* True / False Questions
* Short Answer Questions
* Mixed Question Types

---

## 🎯 Difficulty Levels

Users can select:

* Easy
* Medium
* Hard
* Mixed

---

## 🤖 Machine Learning Models

The system uses four Machine Learning models for question analysis.

| Model               | Purpose                          |
| ------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| SVM                 | Question Type Classification     |
| Logistic Regression | Difficulty Classification        |
| KNN                 | Similarity / Duplicate Detection |
| Random Forest       | Question Quality Classification  |

Character-level TF-IDF features are used to convert question text into numerical representations for Machine Learning classification.

---

## 🔄 System Workflow

```text
Upload Document
       ↓
Extract Text
       ↓
Clean & Normalize Text
       ↓
Detect Language
       ↓
AI Question Generation
       ↓
Question Classification
       ↓
SVM
       ↓
Logistic Regression
       ↓
KNN Similarity Detection
       ↓
Random Forest Quality Classification
       ↓
Display Results
       ↓
Export Questions
```

